med` is set to true, this could lead to significant performance degradation during downsample operations.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java-DST-ADDITION-34566-34726-IfStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"if (mapping.get(\"ignore_malformed\") !\u003d null) {\n                        builder.field(\"ignore_malformed\", mapping.get(\"ignore_malformed\"));\n                    }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"IfStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["mapping","get","builder","field","mapping","get"],"startLine":727,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":729,"endLineOffset":21,"length":161,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java-DST-ADDITION-43574-43884-IfStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"if (sourceIndexMetadata.getSettings().hasValue(FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey())) {\n            builder.put(\n                FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey(),\n                sourceIndexMetadata.getSettings().get(FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey())\n            );\n        }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"IfStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["sourceIndexMetadata","getSettings","hasValue","getKey","builder","put","getKey","sourceIndexMetadata","getSettings","get","getKey"],"startLine":904,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":909,"endLineOffset":9,"length":311,"subs":[]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":909,"line":909,"comment_lines":["[][909]"],"review_comment":["I\u0027m somewhat puzzled by this, so how does `@timestamp` pick up `ignore_above:true` if this is not set? I assume it\u0027s passed somewhere but not everywhere..","I also don\u0027t fully understand this. Maybe the setting came from an index template?","There are two sets of index settings:\r\n1. Settings applied when index is created (what you are looking at).\r\n2. Setting applied _after_ the index is created - everything from the original index is copied (except settings in 1).\r\n\r\nI have to admit i don\u0027t understand the reason for the split but this is the code structure. `FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING` was in 2 but now is in 1. The reason is that by the time 2 is applied it\u0027s too late to \"fix\" mapping of `@timestamp` with it in mind."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","id":35099,"created_at":"2024-12-20T07:48:14Z","original_position":27,"side":"RIGHT","position":27,"submitted_on_commit":"a8335f79231c049065b5445bdac41e60c751c503","diff_hunk":"@@ -897,6 +901,12 @@ private void createDownsampleIndex(\n                 sourceIndexMetadata.getSettings().get(MapperService.INDEX_MAPPING_TOTAL_FIELDS_LIMIT_SETTING.getKey())\n             );\n         }\n+        if (sourceIndexMetadata.getSettings().hasValue(FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey())) {\n+            builder.put(\n+                FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey(),\n+                sourceIndexMetadata.getSettings().get(FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey())\n+            );\n+        }","submitted_line":909},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The Technical Mapping does not specify how the `ignore_malformed` setting should be handled in terms of logging or observability. The current implementation silently applies the setting without any traceable log or metric indicating that this action has been taken. This introduces a blind spot where failures related to this setting cannot be easily traced or diagnosed.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java-DST-A